---
title: Bill Llia Officially Launches Campaign for Governor of Nairobi County
publishedDate: 2026-02-10
source: Nairobi County Press
sourceUrl: https://example.com/bill-llia-launch
excerpt: Healthcare advocate and community leader Dr. Bill Llia has officially launched his campaign for Governor of Nairobi County, promising a platform focused on accessible healthcare, quality education, and sustainable economic growth.
---

NAIROBI — More than 1,000 supporters packed the Nairobi Arena on Saturday as Dr. Bill Llia, a community health advocate with over 12 years of front-line service in the county's most underserved wards, officially declared his candidacy for Governor — vowing to overhaul healthcare, create jobs, and bring clean water to every corner of Nairobi County.

In a charged 30-minute announcement speech, Llia outlined a comprehensive platform built on four pillars: a health centre in every ward, a youth employment and skills programme targeting 10,000 placements within two years, a KES 500 million small business enterprise fund, and a water infrastructure push that promises clean water within one kilometre of every household.

"Nairobi County has tremendous potential, but too many of our people have been left behind by a system that serves the few at the expense of the many," Llia told the crowd, many of whom waved blue campaign banners. "I am running because I believe that every family in this county deserves quality healthcare, clean water, and a real opportunity to build a better life — and I have a plan to deliver all three."

The crowd included community health workers, small business owners, teachers, and youth groups from across the county's eight constituencies. Dozens of first-time voters turned out, underscoring the campaign's focus on engaging young people.

"We are not just launching a campaign — we are building a movement of ordinary citizens who are tired of empty promises and ready for real change," said campaign manager Jane Akinyi. "Bill Llia has spent his career serving Nairobi's communities. He has the experience, the integrity, and the vision to lead this county forward, and we are going to take that message to every doorstep in Nairobi County."

Llia's campaign plans an intensive door-to-door outreach strategy, community barazas in every ward, and a strong digital organising effort to reach younger voters. The campaign is also launching a county-wide petition calling for better healthcare funding that organizers say has already collected over 5,000 signatures.

